			<div class="content" id="post-content-4226736">
									

<p>Ungodly sweet, mildly childish, and possibly saccharine.</p>
<p>Miraculously, it's still alive and isn't causing controversy. Thanks to the folks in IRC like AbsentmindedNihilist, TRutherford, r0se, Jiwoahn, Lordmep, and anyone else who looked in the critters section that I lost record of.</p>
<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/deadly-bread" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3988532); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3988532&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1556650919" alt="Deadly Bread" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3988532)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/deadly-bread" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3988532); return false;">Deadly Bread</a></span> is to thanks for changing the Xs into actual numbers.</p>
<p>Poor execution hindered this piece, and a revision is being done as I'm typing this. With any luck, following the seminar later this week, I'll make this less &quot;please feel emotions&quot; and more evocative, internet willing.</p>
<p>Edit: as of 4/27/19, the focus of this scip has shifted from wholesomeness to &quot;asshole tries to fuck with emotions.&quot;</p>

